        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Emperor Hirohito\n- Concepts: Wet-folding, Shōwa era, Order of the Rising Sun\n\nFacts:\n- Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, which is one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Shōwa was the era name corresponding to Emperor Hirohito's reign, and Shōwa became his own name after his death.",
